.Martin. wrote:
> I've got a few newbie questions about nethack:

Welcome to Nethack and to this newsgroup.

> 1. What can I do with large boxes? How can I open them?

Open them and get any loot deposited there, store your own loot
to be save from monsters picking it up and using it, lock trolls
to prevent them reviving, polymorph them to get an other useful
item, and probably many more. To open them reliably use a key or
a lockpick, a spell or wand if you have, or kick it - but that
may destroy items in the box -, or use a spare weapon to force
the lock.

> 2. What am I supposed to do with potions? I don't know
> what they do? Shall I drink them the moment I pick them up
> or just carry them?

The advanced player will try to identify them first; there are
very cheap scrolls sold in shops for exactly that purpose. If
you're in the mood to just explore the game and don't mind to
kill your character, you may as well dring them. Some potions
can be classified by unicorn horn as well, an other potion can
be identified by an amethyst gemstone. Carrying unidentified
potions is not that good in case you're exposed to fire or cold
(from monsters or traps). A large box (pr a chest) is a good
place to deposit them until you have some identification means.

> 3. What about scrolls? How can I know what each of them does?
> Should I read them the moment I pick them up?

The same as with potions; the advanced player will not read them
unidentified. Have a look at the prices; the cheaper scrolls are
typically useful and uncritical to read - but mind it's status
("BUC status") whether they are blessed, uncursed, or cursed;
the latter is not good as you can guess. Use altars to help you
identify the BUC status, or watch your pet, whether it willingly
or just reluctantly steps on a item on the floor.

> 4. What about weapons: Are particular weapons more
> efficient against certain monsters or it doesn't matter?
> How can I know which weapon to wield against a particular
> monster?

Some weapons hit better and do more damage than other weapons. It
also depends on your weapon proficiency, the better your skill the
better you can use the weapons. The weapon types you can get
skilled in are depending what class you play. Your god may give
you an artifact weapon which has additional powers. There's a lot
more to say about weapons, but for the beginning that may suffice.

> 4a. What does it mean when in my inventory it says, eg:
> long sword (+1) - this (+1) what does it mean?

A bonus; more damage.

> I know there are a lot of questions. I started reading the manual
> but I keep playing in the meantime and those are the questions
> that puzzle me now.
> Thanks for your time 

You're welcome.

In case you want to be spoiled, there's a lot more information
available. But probably you want to find out things yourself to
enjoy the exploration. Keep in mind that, in many cases, you can
apply just common sense to try to solve some issues. If you're
stuck feel free to ask.

